  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mtext>AgN</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mtext>KCl</mtext><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>aq</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mtext>AgCl</mtext><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mtext>KN</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>aq</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math> <br/><br/>Initially there is aq.  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>  solution now as solution of  <math><mtext>AgN</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  is added,  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  is formed. Hence conductivity of solution is almost compensated (or slightly increase) by the formation of  <math><mtext>KN</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> . After end point conductivity increases more rapidly because addition of excess  <math><mtext>AgN</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  solution."
